  "name": "copernicus-glofas-flood-forecast",
  "notes": "The Global Flood Awareness System (GloFAS) is a component of the Copernicus Emergency\nManagement Service providing global hydrological forecasts. This dataset contains daily\nraster GeoTIFFs derived from ECMWF ensemble streamflow predictions.\n\nReturn period exceedance layers show the probability (%) that river discharge will exceed\nthe 5-year or 20-year return period threshold at any point within the forecast horizon.\nFlood summary layers combine 2-, 5-, and 20-year exceedance probabilities into categorical\nflood alert information for different forecast windows (days 1-3, 4-10, 11-15).\n\nRapidFloodMapping and RapidImpactAssessment are experimental products providing estimated\nflood extent at 1 km resolution and potential impact on population and land use.",
